{"id":"pkg/router/metrics.go:(*routerMetrics).instrument","summary":"Watches are now counted in a long-running gauge and excluded from the duration histogram and in-flight gauge. The histogram gains a verb label, so existing series and queries change shape.","issues":[{"severity":"medium","title":"Verb label is unbounded for arbitrary HTTP methods","evidence":"verb := requestVerb(req) ... WithLabelValues(metricGroup, verb, strconv.Itoa(rec.status))","failure_scenario":"A client sends requests with distinct custom methods (FOO1, FOO2, ...) to any path. requestVerb falls back to strings.ToLower(req.Method), and the apiserver RequestInfoFactory leaves unknown methods as the lowercased method, so each one creates a new histogram series. This defeats the unknown-group label that exists to stop client-chosen series.","introduced_by_pr":true,"depends_on_unseen_code":true,"line":78}],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Watches leave latency histogram; histogram gains verb label","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Changes the metric label schema and the request accounting and logging path, including defer ordering for watches.","risk_signals":["metric label schema changed","metric cardinality","defer ordering"],"focus":["verb label cardinality for non-standard HTTP methods","dashboards and alerts using http_request_duration_seconds that lack the verb label","access log still written exactly once per watch, including on panic"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:type GrafanaRouter","summary":"Adds a router-wide context and cancel func used to end all watches on shutdown.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"GrafanaRouter gets a router-wide watch context","confidence":0.7,"reason":"Adds fields only; behavior lives in serveWatch and closeWatches.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:(*GrafanaRouter).HandleFunc","summary":"Upgrade requests to routed groups now get a 400, and watch requests run through serveWatch with the entry's scope so they end when the backend is replaced or the router closes. Other requests are unchanged.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Routed watches get cancelable scope; upgrades rejected with 400","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Changes request handling, adds rejection of upgrade requests and concurrency/lifecycle control of streaming requests.","risk_signals":["concurrency","request lifetime","new 400 response","behavior change for upgrade requests"],"focus":["rejectUpgrade applies to all verbs, not only watches; confirm no client legitimately sends Connection: Upgrade to routed groups","watch ended by router yields a clean stream end and the breaker records the right outcome","entry.watches is always non-nil for entries in the snapshot"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:(*GrafanaRouter).serveUnregisteredGroup","summary":"The single-tenant fallback path now rejects upgrades with a 400 and serves watches via serveWatch with only the router-wide shutdown scope. Such watches are not ended on backend changes.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Fallback path rejects upgrades and wraps watches","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Changes request handling and lifetime of streaming requests on the fallback path.","risk_signals":["concurrency","request lifetime","new 400 response"],"focus":["upgrade rejection for the unregistered-group fallback in middleware mode","watches here end only on shutdown or client disconnect"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/watch.go","summary":"New file that identifies watch requests via the apiserver RequestInfoFactory, rejects upgrades, and runs watches under a cancelable context tied to the backend scope and router shutdown. It recovers ErrAbortHandler panics when the router ended the watch itself, so the client sees a clean end.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add watch lifecycle: verb detection, upgrade rejection, cancellation","confidence":0.9,"reason":"New concurrency, context cancellation and panic-recovery logic on the request path.","risk_signals":["concurrency","panic recovery","context cancellation","request lifetime"],"focus":["recover swallows ErrAbortHandler only when the router canceled and the client did not; check other abort causes still propagate","AfterFunc cleanup so no goroutine or context leaks per watch","requestVerb fallback for unknown paths and methods"]}
]}

