{"id":"pkg/router/metrics.go:(*routerMetrics).instrument","summary":"Watches are now counted in a long-running gauge and excluded from the in-flight gauge and duration histogram. The histogram gains a verb label, which changes the exported series shape and dashboards or alerts that use it.","issues":[{"severity":"medium","title":"Unbounded verb label allows metric cardinality growth","evidence":"if err != nil || info.Verb == \"\" { return strings.ToLower(req.Method) } ... WithLabelValues(metricGroup, verb, strconv.Itoa(rec.status))","failure_scenario":"A client sends requests with arbitrary HTTP methods (e.g. FOO1, FOO2, ...) to any path, including unknown groups. Each distinct lowercased method becomes a new verb label value and a new native-histogram series, although the group label is bounded to prevent exactly this.","introduced_by_pr":true,"depends_on_unseen_code":false}],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Watches leave the histogram and in-flight gauge; verb label added","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Changes metric semantics and labels, request flow and defer ordering, and the logging path for watches.","risk_signals":["metric label schema changed","new label cardinality","defer/panic ordering"],"focus":["dashboards and alerts using http_request_duration_seconds without the verb label","verb label cardinality for arbitrary methods","watch access log still emitted on panic or abort"]},
